From d576f5b65b2adced6b1a8defb9e0e8157585cf1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Franck <franck.bailleux@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 10:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: align schemas, add tests, pyproject.toml and env.example
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- jean_marc.py: align all field names with Jean-Marc Pydantic schema 2.0
  (observed_steps 0-based, real UUIDs, irritant_kind enums, gap_description,
  total_irritant_severity, procedure_state enum, TheFabric->Jean-Marc translators)
- bundlefabric.py: fix TPS key — handle both freshness (real manifests) and
  freshness_score (TheFabric bundles); same fix for updated_at vs last_updated
- pyspur.py + engine.py: LLM model configurable via --pyspur-model / PYSPUR_MODEL
- cli.py: add --pyspur-model, --pyspur-url (live submission), --output defaults
  to ./artifacts, warns when bundlefabric dir is missing
- pyproject.toml: package metadata, entry point, zero runtime deps, dev extras
- .env.example: document KFABRIC_URL, KFABRIC_API_KEY, PYSPUR_URL, PYSPUR_MODEL
- tests/: 49 tests for session_analysis, jean_marc schema, bundlefabric scoring
